{"availability":"available","full":"jeromepl/rails-react-server-components-demo","name":"rails-react-server-components-demo","description":"React Server Components's \"Notes\" demo but with a Ruby on Rails backend(!)","category":"Productivity","language":"Ruby","stars":8,"forks":1,"created":"2023-10-16T02:17:35Z","updated":"2024-04-01T19:40:36Z","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["rails","react","server-components"],"demo":"https://twitter.com/acdlite","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:42.243Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:42.243Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T01:47:42.243Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T01:25:53.878Z","stars":8,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-08T04:50:56.322Z","stars":8,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-10T11:05:49.214Z","stars":8,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-15T21:47:09.195Z","stars":8,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-20T01:47:42.243Z","stars":8,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I am working on a blog post to go into more details about how this works. Stay tuned!","This repo is a demo of how React Server Components can be used in other backend languages than NodeJS. It reproduces the React server-components-demo and reuses most of its front-end code but with a Ruby on Rails back-end.","It works as a regular Rails app with a bundled javascript front-end (through shackapaker), except that the /notes route renders the page in React's special \"RSC wire format\" and streams it to the front-end. This is in essence mimicking what React's renderToPipeableStream NodeJS API does."],"features":["The ability to send to the front-end instructions to not just render specific React components, but also render them with HTML or even other React components as children.","Streaming components as they become available and making use of React's Suspense to show a fallback while waiting for the result."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jeromepl/rails-react-server-components-demo/blob/main/R